message: "If you use this research prototype, please cite the software using these metadata."
title: "DIAS: Dynamic and Explainable Access Control for Blockchain-enabled Inter-organizational Data Sharing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rayudu"
    given-names: "Alapati Venkat"
    email: "venkatarayudu_alapati@srmap.edu.in"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, SRM University-AP"
  - family-names: "Sengupta"
    given-names: "Tirthankar"
    email: "tirthankar.s@srmap.edu.in"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, SRM University-AP"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-26
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A Hyperledger Fabric research prototype for access control among five synthetic
  criminal-justice organizations: an exact-scope dynamic authorization grants a
  matching request automatically; otherwise an application-backend LLM gives an
  advisory recommendation and an auditor makes the binding decision, with the
  request and the decision (including agreement with the LLM) recorded on the
  ledger.
keywords:
  - Hyperledger Fabric
  - explainable access control
  - dynamic authorization
  - large language models
  - blockchain audit
  - inter-agency data sharing
